.IX Title "Lucy::Search::Collector::BitCollector 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Search::Collector::BitCollector 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Search::Collector::BitCollector \- Collector which records doc nums in a BitVector.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 10
\&    my $bit_vec = Lucy::Object::BitVector\->new(
\&        capacity => $searcher\->doc_max + 1,
\&    );
\&    my $bit_collector = Lucy::Search::Collector::BitCollector\->new(
\&        bit_vector => $bit_vec, 
\&    );
\&    $searcher\->collect(
\&        collector => $bit_collector,
\&        query     => $query,
\&    );
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
BitCollector is a Collector which saves matching document ids in a
BitVector.  It is useful for recording the
entire set of documents which matches a query.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $bit_collector = Lucy::Search::Collector::BitCollector\->new(
\&        bit_vector => $bit_vec,    # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new BitCollector.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBbit_vector\fR \- A Lucy::Object::BitVector.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS collect
.IX Subsection "collect"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_collector\->collect($doc_id);
.Ve
.PP
Set bit in the object’s BitVector for the supplied doc id.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Search::Collector::BitCollector isa Lucy::Search::Collector isa Clownfish::Obj.
